{"id": "EUVD-2026-103546", "enisaUuid": "65131f9b-7be7-3df0-9901-7fbd54ebf424", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: mgmt: Dequeue pending mesh_send_sync entries on cancel\n\nIn send_cancel(), pending mesh_tx objects are removed from the\nhdev->mesh_pending list and freed via mesh_send_complete().  However, if\na mesh transmission was already queued onto hdev->cmd_sync_work_list via\nmesh_next(), the queued entry retains a raw pointer to mesh_tx.\n\nWhen hci_cmd_sync_work later processes the entry, it attempts to execute\nmesh_send_sync and its destroy callback mesh_send_start_complete using\nthe already freed mesh_tx pointer, leading to a use-after-free.\n\nFix this by invoking hci_cmd_sync_dequeue() for mesh_send_sync on the\ntarget mesh_tx before completing it.  If the entry is found and dequeued,\nits destroy callback will complete and free the object; otherwise,\nmesh_send_complete() is called directly.\n\nAdditionally, ensure the transmission queue advances after cancellation\nor errors.  In mesh_send_start_complete(), call mesh_next() on error\nunless err is -ECANCELED, because hci_cmd_sync_dequeue() holds\nhdev->cmd_sync_work_lock and calling mesh_next() synchronously would\ndeadlock.  Instead, advance the queue in send_cancel() once the lock is\nreleased and if no transmission is in progress.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:19:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:23:00", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f84e52829021d00bca8e067302f597c71af1f71a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/718a8ffa180d469f99ad4f746f00cafd39456415", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/084be90948632a5a358821e687b11a14445aae76", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2189a219397d8e73808a67c4aade837b635705da", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/03ced4687fb79286be7fdee0fc58d2c74de3e7bb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/71af682ba4692c2ed9ace4c3d4ca462ae368c029"], "aliases": ["GHSA-qvq7-5mpj-hvwr", "CVE-2026-98632"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0fb1c84a-8a56-3ca2-b6c9-d65517f130cb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "11073b69-2f81-39ff-9252-f1a8ce15c9a2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b338d91703fae6f6afd67f3f75caa3b8f36ddef3 <2189a219397d8e73808a67c4aade837b635705da"}, {"id": "30f0cb00-5a2c-3dca-8089-773d148f1d6f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "56d98a39-c4f9-3783-b947-a694d2e01619", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "6f72b40b-599b-399c-8d3d-e181053133bc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b338d91703fae6f6afd67f3f75caa3b8f36ddef3 <f84e52829021d00bca8e067302f597c71af1f71a"}, {"id": "aeb7f7c1-4883-3064-9fea-ca067c8902b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1"}, {"id": "aee1d7ab-39f1-3806-b05d-7d681b27d14b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "af1cce98-6cd3-361e-b546-e35195d57563", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b338d91703fae6f6afd67f3f75caa3b8f36ddef3 <03ced4687fb79286be7fdee0fc58d2c74de3e7bb"}, {"id": "d4445d74-6498-397c-b142-5e7dd8dfadc2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "e13f469e-f958-30ce-b1a4-c57c615f61c9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b338d91703fae6f6afd67f3f75caa3b8f36ddef3 <084be90948632a5a358821e687b11a14445aae76"}, {"id": "e1cf3355-1884-331b-b0d9-e758d4c441d6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "e7e24ef2-93c1-31b4-9d2e-48162d6e37ed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b338d91703fae6f6afd67f3f75caa3b8f36ddef3 <718a8ffa180d469f99ad4f746f00cafd39456415"}, {"id": "e90388f0-064f-307c-9c83-e45642c6cb39", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b338d91703fae6f6afd67f3f75caa3b8f36ddef3 <71af682ba4692c2ed9ace4c3d4ca462ae368c029"}, {"id": "ecde4af6-1d26-31a5-ab92-fa6b2bb432d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "678e9a0e-ccc4-32a0-a4e0-208c46ee7730", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}